00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:57.441
Yeah, we didn't want to just trust the AWS

625
00:21:57.481 --> 00:21:58.922
benchmark, so we built our own.

626
00:21:59.182 --> 00:22:01.483
And I think it's fairly comprehensive,

627
00:22:01.523 --> 00:22:03.384
probably more comprehensive than it needed to

628
00:22:03.444 --> 00:22:03.564
be.

629
00:22:04.365 --> 00:22:06.086
And it's a bit like what we've done before for

630
00:22:06.106 --> 00:22:06.246
other

631
00:22:07.978 --> 00:22:09.079
optimization stories.

632
00:22:09.159 --> 00:22:11.580
We built a CDK application, CDK application,

633
00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:14.142
that deploys the infrastructure, repeatedly

634
00:22:14.522 --> 00:22:18.184
launches ECS tasks, and measures performance in

635
00:22:18.364 --> 00:22:19.205
a few different dimensions.

636
00:22:19.965 --> 00:22:23.047
The workload was a Python application using the

637
00:22:23.107 --> 00:22:25.308
Python 3.12 slim actually base image.

638
00:22:26.088 --> 00:22:29.410
The application imports and uses its dependency.

639
00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:31.392
So we're testing realistic files, we think,

640
00:22:31.492 --> 00:22:33.133
rather than artificially bloated images.

641
00:22:33.733 --> 00:22:35.394
And then we have two image variants.

642
00:22:35.414 --> 00:22:37.215
A small one was just NumPy and Pandas.

643
00:22:37.634 --> 00:22:39.095
and a large one, which has a lot of big

644
00:22:39.135 --> 00:22:41.336
dependencies, PyTorch and Scikit-learn,

645
00:22:41.596 --> 00:22:43.637
PyRO and Transformers.

646
00:22:44.478 --> 00:22:48.260
So the variables we tested were, we did x86-64

647
00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:49.460
and ARM64.

648
00:22:50.041 --> 00:22:52.082
We had the two image sizes, and then we had

649
00:22:52.102 --> 00:22:55.303
three compression values, gzip, zstandard and

650
00:22:55.464 --> 00:22:55.944
uncompressed.

651
00:22:56.524 --> 00:22:58.785
And then we had Soci, either enabled or

652
00:22:58.825 --> 00:23:00.126
disabled, where supported.

653
00:23:01.407 --> 00:23:04.488
We also tested in Fargate and ECS on EC2.

654
00:23:05.289 --> 00:23:07.290
And just for kicks, we also tried

655
00:23:07.891 --> 00:23:12.311
two different OSs for EC2, Amazon Linux 2023,

656
00:23:12.394 --> 00:23:13.255
and Bottlerocket.

657
00:23:14.355 --> 00:23:16.016
So not every combination is possible.

