00:23:23.882 --> 00:23:25.763
But overall, that gives us 44 different

662
00:23:25.883 --> 00:23:26.543
permutations.

663
00:23:26.944 --> 00:23:28.425
We ran each one 30 times each,

664
00:23:29.245 --> 00:23:32.928
and that gives us 1,320 task executions.

665
00:23:33.428 --> 00:23:35.229
All of them were using one vCPU and two

666
00:23:35.249 --> 00:23:36.290
gigabytes of memory.

667
00:23:37.692 --> 00:23:40.435
So how we measured it is we used ECS timestamps

668
00:23:40.635 --> 00:23:41.997
to calculate the pull time.

669
00:23:42.437 --> 00:23:46.041
So you can get all of that information from ECS,

670
00:23:46.061 --> 00:23:49.805
like how long it takes to do image retrieval,

671
00:23:50.166 --> 00:23:52.328
the container startup time from task creation to

672
00:23:52.368 --> 00:23:53.409
